make sure you guys hit the subscribe  button if you guys are enjoying the  content that we're throwing up and uh  make sure you guys hit the like button  if you enjoy the video and yeah  let's begin  what's going on guys this is rob and we  are back again with another installment  of our beyond omega level series where  we discuss the most powerful characters  in comics and today we are breaking down  a character that is relatively obscure  having only appeared in about three  issues but who is arguably the second  most powerful character in marvel comics  yes this guy is arguably more powerful  than the living tribunal and of course  the character that i'm talking about is  the fulcrum created by daniel noff and  charles noff and first appearing in  eternals number seven in 2009. but  before we get into the fulcrum's first  appearance we need to establish what was  going on with the eternals at the time  and at this point the eternals basically  found themselves in the middle of a  civil war with one side including icarus  makari and cersei who were loyal to  their leader xeros and the other side  who had rebelled against xeros which  included druid and gilgamesh who'd  basically been brainwashed by druid to  murder makari now druid can also destroy  the eternal's activation chambers which  takes away their immortality and so when  makari dies a failsafe is triggered that  will end with all life on earth being  destroyed by an army of cosmic creatures  called the horde now out of desperation  cersei sacrifices herself to resurrect  makari because without him the eternals  cannot communicate with the celestials  and she finds herself in the afterlife  sitting at a bar and talking to a  bartender named jack who informs her  that she is not in heaven or hell but in  a place called the vestibule now he  explains that this is sort of a holding  place for eternals when they die and  either wait to be reborn in an  activation chamber or go on to the place  called lacuna which sounds like the  final destination for the souls of  eternals but it's merely speculation  because jack refuses to describe it with  any more detail now when we see a  conversation between the dreaming  celestial and huawei to the watcher the  dreaming celestial had basically been  visited by makari and it told him that  the preliminary horde was on its way to  earth and he tells uwatu that he is now  experiencing emotions which is not  compatible with his mandate now this  would normally mean that he needed to  shut himself down and compress himself  into a black hole but he says he cannot  do that because he needs to get vital  information concerning earth to the  fulcrum himself but offers no additional  details as to who or what the fulcrum is  now back on earth icarus has gone rogue  and picks a fight with druid in  violation of a treaty that had been  agreed to by drury and zuros now icarus  gets druik's forces to follow him to  alcatraz island which at that time is  where the x-men lived and they joined  the battle on icarus's side in what  seems to be a way to justify putting  wolverine on the cover of the next  eternals issue to basically try and sell  more copies of a book that was about to  get cancelled but anyway the x-men who  really shouldn't be able to put up much  of a fight against the eternals are  actually able to hold their own because  of teamwork i guess but that's really  not that important to the overall story  back in space the dreaming celestial is  confronted by the horde which is making  its way to earth now the celestial tells  the horror that if it tries to attack  him the horde will be punished by the  fulcrum but the horde responds by saying  that the fulcrum will actually punish  the celestial if he doesn't stand aside  so from this exchange we see that the  fulcrum seems to be pulling the strings  of this whole event and that both the  dreaming celestial and the horde are  simply carrying out a plan that was set  in place by the fulcrum and furthermore  that both of these extremely powerful  entities are at the mercy of the fulcrum  that he could destroy any of them if he  wished is a testament to how powerful he  is so the celestial informs the horde  that the amount of life force energy on  earth would exceed the maximum storage  within the horde if it were to harvest  the planet and that if the horde  proceeds with its plan all matter in  this quadrant of the galaxy would simply  be destroyed now the horde then decides  that it will proceed towards earth  anyway bypassing its storage and  channeling all energy it absorbs to the  all high fulcrum the celestial then goes  to inform the fulcrum of the horde's  decision and the horde arrives on earth  which forces the eternals to stop  fighting amongst themselves and turn  their attention to the horde before it  destroys all life on earth as not even  celestials are able to stop them and so  to do this they decide they need to come  together to form the unimine which will  allow them to take over the body of the  dreaming celestial in order to do that  however the eternals have to select a  prime eternal and when xeros shows up  with the rest of the group they decide  to make icarus the prime eternal and the  unimine takes over the dreaming  celestial's body but while this goes on  the celestial's consciousness is still  talking to uwatu who informs the  celestial that he has developed free  will which he uses to allow the unimine  to inhabit his body to fight the horde  while his consciousness goes to appeal  directly to the fulcrum and spare earth  now when we see the dreaming celestial  enter the vestibule and start talking  with jack the bartender who's revealed  to actually be the fulcrum he tells the  fulcrum about the changes to his  programming his development of emotions  and a conscience and asked the fulcrum  to spare earth from the horde now the  fulcrum agrees on the condition that the  celestial can answer two questions the  first simply being why to which the  celestial responds because i care and  the fulcrum commends tiamou for being  the first in the history of time to ever  ascend to question the fulcrum's will  and become a free-thinking celestial he  then declares the celestial to be as  equal and asks his second question which  is whether the celestial will come with  him to destroy the horde and then we get  to see this epic battle with the fulcrum  and the dreaming celestial fighting side  by side to take down the world devouring  horde just kidding we've seen nothing  the story jumps forward over a hundred  years into the future with the eternals  once again in hiding however one of them  joey athena the son of the eternal  athena has been located by michelle  urich the granddaughter of the daily  bugle reporter ben urich and he just  tells her that the fulcrum restored all  the damage done by the horde and set  everything right and that no one even  remembered the horde's attack and that's  really all we know about the fulcrum  because like i said he's only appeared  in three issues that make up this story  arc now some have theorized that the  fulcrum is actually not a separate  entity but instead is simply one aspect  of the one above all and they point to  the fact that he takes the form of a man  named jack and the one above all was  once depicted as being jack kirby but  there's really nothing in these issues  that indicates the fulcrum has anything  to do with the one above all except  maybe that he is referred to as the all  high by the horde but either way the  fact that he is pretty much omnipotent  in the sense that the celestials and the  horde both of which are cosmically  powerful beings answer directly to him  earns him a spot on our beyond omega  level series but with that being said  let me know what you guys think right do  you want to see more of the fulcrum do  you think he should appear more i'm kind  of curious maybe i think he's one of  those characters who just needed to be a  one-off and that's it there's no real  purpose in having his character return  but let me know what you guys think  thank you all for watching and i will  catch you all later  peace

